<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-3> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-3>;
  dc:date "August 2025";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/653EF82D99E63E11A490F9BB95D7C9"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087>;
  schema:text "[Image: table or graph comparing SE values for FPG and HDL across groups and studies] In all 3 studies, the SE values for “adjusted change” of FPG (mg/dL) are 1.7 for both control and treated groups. Similarly, the SE values for HDL adjusted change are 1.3 in all 6 groups (across 3 studies). In each of the 3 studies, control and treated groups have different means, but identical SE values across all measures. (expression of concern)";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.1016%2Fj.jacl.2015.12.017>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-4> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-4>;
  dc:date "September 2025";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/653EF82D99E63E11A490F9BB95D7C9"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087>;
  schema:text "Update of #2: The reason the control and treated groups have identical SE values is that ANCOVA generates a single pooled error variance. While not statistically “wrong,” this mode of presentation can be misleading — it prevents readers from assessing the actual within-group and between-group variabilities in the dataset. The authors are encouraged to share raw data, and group-specific SE data.";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.1016%2Fj.jacl.2015.12.017>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA233158DEF9C3F087-inspectai-1-2> .

