<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-1> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-1>;
  dc:date "November 2021";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/9E6CC04E60666CB9B82318B1587C06"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  schema:text "October 2021 retraction: \"The journal retracts the article, Effects of a Single Dose of Ivermectin on Viral and Clinical Outcomes in Asymptomatic SARS-CoV-2 Infected Subjects: A Pilot Clinical Trial in Lebanon [1], cited above. Following publication, the authors contacted the editorial office regarding an error between files used for the statistical analysis. Adhering to our complaints procedure, an investigation was conducted that confirmed the error reported by the authors. This retraction was approved by the Editor in Chief of the journal. The authors agreed to this retraction.\" Retraction Watch coverage: Also see this BBC article from October 2021: From that article: \"A recent study in Lebanon was found to have blocks of details of 11 patients that had been copied and pasted repeatedly - suggesting many of the trial's apparent patients didn't really exist.\"";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.3390%2Fv13060989>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-2> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-2>;
  dc:date "November 2021";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/9E6CC04E60666CB9B82318B1587C06"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  schema:text "Independent investigations by the team, institutional and the journal review ALL confirmed that there was no ethical violation. It was a simple error in the files used for the analysis. The authors had the moral and professional courage to retract the paper. Adding comments on pubpeer will be construed as though there were ethical violations. This site is intended to uncover or question data that may appear to have been falsified, fabricated or obtained via unethical routes. None of these are in this paper. So, keeping this comment will tarnish the reputation of the authors for no valid reason. Thank you.";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.3390%2Fv13060989>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-3> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-3>;
  dc:date "November 2021";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/9E6CC04E60666CB9B82318B1587C06"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68>;
  schema:text "#2 How could the journal confirm that errors in the data were accidental? Have the editors announced this finding? It is not in the Retraction Note. _\"This site is intended to uncover or question data that may appear to have been falsified, fabricated or obtained via unethical routes\"_ I cannot speak for the intentions of PubPeer's architects, but I don't believe this is true. People often leave comments about innocent errors in figure assembly, or even to comment positively on papers that deserve wider attention or have corollaries that deserve further exploration.";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.3390%2Fv13060989>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEA3F7A45FD29B97F68-inspectai-1-2> .

