<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-2> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-2>;
  dc:date "August 2025";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/653EF82D99E63E11A490F9BB95D7C9"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  schema:text """[Image: Chart or data image from the publication]
The two groups have identical SE values across all parameters. I understand that the means reflect the difference between data taken before and after the intervention period.""";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.1016%2Fj.jacl.2015.12.017>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-3> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-3>;
  dc:date "August 2025";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/653EF82D99E63E11A490F9BB95D7C9"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  schema:text """[Image: Chart or data image from the publication]
In all 3 studies, the SE values for “adjusted change” of FPG (mg/dL) are 1.7 for both control and treated groups. Similarly, the SE values for HDL adjusted change are 1.3 in all 6 groups (across 3 studies). In each of the 3 studies, control and treated groups have different means, but identical SE values across all measures. (expression of concern)""";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.1016%2Fj.jacl.2015.12.017>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-4> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-4>;
  dc:date "September 2025";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/653EF82D99E63E11A490F9BB95D7C9"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
  prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/evidence-aggregation/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  prov:wasMemberOf <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/research-integrity-assessment/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83>;
  schema:text "Update of #2: The reason the control and treated groups have identical SE values is that ANCOVA generates a single pooled error variance. While not statistically “wrong,” this mode of presentation can be misleading — it prevents readers from assessing the actual within-group and between-group variabilities in the dataset. The authors are encouraged to share raw data, and group-specific SE data.";
  ripe:concerns <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/work/10.1016%2Fj.jacl.2015.12.017>;
  tido:supports <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-human-1-2>,
    <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/integrity-assessment-hypothesis/RIPEAF7E1928294A86E83-inspectai-1-2> .

<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/peer-comment/RIPEAF8D7B98E670B0858-1> a ripe:PeerComment;
  dc:creator <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/author/pubpeer-RIPEAF8D7B98E670B0858-1>;
  dc:date "August 2021";
  fabio:hasURL "https://pubpeer.com/publications/6E7031A842CC900FC7D513986AC9BF"^^xsd:anyURI;
  prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-kg/source/pubpeer>;
